              "readme": "# Celigo AI\n\nOne-stop shop for building integrations on the [Celigo](https://www.celigo.com) platform with AI.\n\n[![skills.sh](https://skills.sh/b/celigo/ai)](https://skills.sh/celigo/ai)\n\nThis repo contains:\n\n- **[Skills](#skills)** -- domain knowledge for AI coding assistants (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, and [50+ more](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills#compatibility))\n- **[MCP Prompts & Resources](#mcp-prompts--resources)** -- content served by the Celigo MCP server\n\n## Install Skills\n\n```bash\nnpx skills add celigo/ai\n```\n\n### Install specific skills\n\n```bash\n# List available skills\nnpx skills add celigo/ai --list\n\n# Install one skill\nnpx skills add celigo/ai --skill getting-started\n\n# Install to a specific agent\nnpx skills add celigo/ai --skill configuring-exports -a claude-code\n```\n\n## Install as a Plugin\n\nThis repo is also a native plugin marketplace for Claude Code and Cursor, bundling all of the skills below plus the Celigo Platform MCP server.\n\n**[Claude Code](https://code.claude.com)** -- in the app, or with the `claude` CLI:\n\n```\n/plugin marketplace add celigo/ai\n/plugin install celigo@celigo\n```\n\n**[Cursor](https://cursor.com)** -- install **Celigo** from the Cursor plugin marketplace (Settings -> Plugins). Team admins can add this repo directly under Team Marketplaces.\n\n**[Codex](https://developers.openai.com/codex)** -- run `codex plugin marketplace add celigo/ai`, then install **celigo** from the Plugins Directory in the ChatGPT desktop app.\n\nFor [50+ other agents](https://github.com/vercel-labs/skills#compatibility), use the [skills install](#install-skills) above.\n\nInstalling the plugin also configures the **Celigo Platform MCP server** (`https://api.integrator.io/celigo-mcp`). It authenticates via OAuth -- the first time an agent uses it, you'll be prompted to sign in to Celigo, so no API token is required.\n\nThe plugin ships the **US** endpoint. Each region runs its own identity provider, so if your account lives in the **EU**, **AU**, or **CA**, the sign-in won't complete against it -- configure your region's endpoint by hand instead (`https://api.eu.integrator.io/celigo-mcp`, `https://api.au.integrator.io/celigo-mcp`, or `https://api.ca.integrator.io/celigo-mcp`). See [Regions](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/docs/connect-mcp.md#regions).\n\nUsing a different client -- VS Code, Windsurf, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, or Claude Desktop? See **[Connect the Celigo MCP server](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/docs/connect-mcp.md)** for copy-paste config and a one-click *Add to Cursor* button.\n\n## Skills\n\nSkill how-tos show `celigo` CLI commands, but most operations map directly to the bundled Celigo Platform MCP server's tools (`list_*` / `upsert_*` / `delete_resource` / `run_flow` / `deploy_template`), so agents connected over MCP follow the same skills and translate the command blocks. A few admin surfaces (the local account index, API tokens, stacks, on-premise agents, users) remain CLI/REST/UI-only.\n\n| Skill | Description |\n|---|---|\n| [getting-started](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/getting-started) | Core concepts, build order, account discovery, and which skill to use |\n| [configuring-connections](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-connections) | Credentials, auth methods, OAuth, iClients |\n| [configuring-exports](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-exports) | Data source steps -- REST, SOAP, database, file, webhook, delta sync |\n| [configuring-imports](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-imports) | Data destination steps -- mappings, lookups, upsert logic |\n| [building-flows](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/building-flows) | Pipelines wiring exports to imports -- scheduling, chaining, error management |\n| [building-apis](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/building-apis) | Custom HTTP endpoints for synchronous external access |\n| [building-tools](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/building-tools) | Reusable operations callable from flows, APIs, agents, and MCP servers |\n| [building-mcp-servers](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/building-mcp-servers) | MCP endpoints exposing tools to external AI agents |\n| [building-b2b](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/building-b2b) | EDI integrations -- trading partners, X12/EDIFACT, file definitions |\n| [configuring-ai-agents](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-ai-agents) | LLM-powered import steps (OpenAI, Gemini) and guardrails |\n| [configuring-filters](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-filters) | Expression and script filters on exports, imports, and branches |\n| [configuring-guardrails](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-guardrails) | PII detection, content moderation, AI-based validation |\n| [configuring-lookup-caches](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/configuring-lookup-caches) | In-memory key-value stores for fast lookups and dedup |\n| [managing-users](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/managing-users) | User invitations, permissions, MFA/SSO, access levels |\n| [managing-integrations](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/managing-integrations) | Integration containers, cloning, and lifecycle management (ILM) across environments |\n| [managing-api-tokens](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/managing-api-tokens) | Inbound API tokens -- scoping, rotation, revoke/delete lifecycle |\n| [managing-stacks](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/managing-stacks) | Bring-your-own compute for hooks and connector wrappers (server or AWS Lambda) |\n| [managing-on-premise-agents](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/managing-on-premise-agents) | Secure connectivity to private systems behind a firewall |\n| [using-marketplace-templates](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/using-marketplace-templates) | Install Templates and Integration Apps; copy prebuilt flows |\n| [troubleshooting-flows](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/troubleshooting-flows) | Diagnosing failures, partial errors, stuck jobs, empty runs |\n| [writing-mappings](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/writing-mappings) | Mapper 2.0, Transformation 2.0, lookups, response mapping |\n| [writing-handlebars](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/writing-handlebars) | Dynamic template expressions for mappings, URIs, SQL, filters |\n| [writing-scripts](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/writing-scripts) | JavaScript hooks -- preSavePage, preMap, postMap, postSubmit |\n| [writing-sql](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/skills/writing-sql) | SQL for RDBMS exports/imports across Snowflake, Postgres, MySQL, and more |\n\n## Slash Commands\n\nThe plugin bundles slash commands for Cursor and Claude Code -- skills-backed authoring helpers that work without a connected account:\n\n| Command | Description |\n|---|---|\n| `/celigo-plan-integration` | Plan a new integration from requirements (design + build order) |\n| `/celigo-handlebars` | Author or debug a Handlebars expression |\n| `/celigo-sql` | Write SQL for an RDBMS export/import |\n| `/celigo-mapping` | Build a field mapping (Mapper 2.0) |\n| `/celigo-review-config` | Review a pasted resource config against best practices |\n\n## MCP Prompts & Resources\n\nThe [`mcp/`](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp) directory contains prompts and resources served by the Celigo MCP server via the MCP protocol's `prompts/list`, `prompts/get`, `resources/list`, and `resources/read` endpoints.\n\n### Prompts\n\n| Prompt | Description |\n|---|---|\n| [getting-started](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/getting-started.md) | Orientation for the Celigo MCP server -- core concepts, build order, tool inventory |\n| [plan-new-integration](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/plan-new-integration.md) | Plan a new integration from requirements |\n| [review-flow-config](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/review-flow-config.md) | Review an existing flow configuration |\n| [troubleshoot-flow](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/troubleshoot-flow.md) | Diagnose a failing or misbehaving flow |\n| [diagnose-connection](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/diagnose-connection.md) | Troubleshoot connection issues |\n| [audit-account-health](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/audit-account-health.md) | Audit account health and find issues |\n| [writing-handlebars](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/writing-handlebars.md) | Write Handlebars template expressions |\n| [writing-sql](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/prompts/writing-sql.md) | Write SQL for RDBMS exports and imports |\n\n### Resources\n\n| Resource | URI |\n|---|---|\n| [Account Architecture Model](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/account-architecture.md) | `celigo://resources/account-architecture` |\n| [Account Settings Reference](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/account-settings.md) | `celigo://resources/account-settings` |\n| [API Reference](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/api-reference.md) | `celigo://resources/api-reference` |\n| [Connector Catalog](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/connector-catalog.md) | `celigo://resources/connector-catalog` |\n| [Error Patterns](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/error-patterns.md) | `celigo://resources/error-patterns` |\n| [Glossary](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/glossary.md) | `celigo://resources/glossary` |\n| [Handlebars Helper Catalog](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/handlebars-helpers.md) | `celigo://resources/handlebars-helpers` |\n| [Recycle Bin Reference](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/recycle-bin.md) | `celigo://resources/recycle-bin` |\n| [Tool Usage Guide](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/resources/tool-usage-guide.md) | `celigo://resources/tool-usage-guide` |\n\n### Adding MCP content\n\nSee the [MCP README](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/mcp/README.md) for the frontmatter schema and how the Celigo MCP server consumes these files.\n\n## Celigo CLI\n\nThe skills reference the [Celigo CLI](https://www.npmjs.com/package/celigo-cli) for examples. Install it with:\n\n```bash\nnpm install -g celigo-cli\n```\n\nAPI and UI alternatives are noted where applicable.\n\n## Links\n\n- [Celigo Documentation](https://docs.celigo.com)\n- [Celigo Developer Guide](https://developer.celigo.com)\n- [Agent Skills Specification](https://agentskills.io)\n- [Skills Directory](https://skills.sh)\n\n## License\n\n[MIT](https://github.com/celigo/ai/blob/main/LICENSE)\n",
